.TH CLEAR 1 UniSoft
.SH NAME
clear \- clear terminal screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Clear\^
clears your screen if this is possible.
It looks in the environment for the terminal type
(\f3TERM\f1) and capabilities string (\f3TERMCAP\f1).
If \f3TERMCAP\f1 is not found in the environment,
it looks in
.B /etc/termcap
to figure out how to clear the screen.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
clear
.PP
clears the screen.
.SH FILES
.ta \w'/etc/termcap\ \ \ \ \ 'u
/etc/termcap	terminal capability data base
.SH "SEE ALSO"
environ(4), termcap(5)
.DT
